Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the Software Engineer, Applied AI (FDE) role at Attune. I bring more than three years of software engineering experience delivering production backend systems, agentic workflows, third-party integrations, and data pipelines. Attune's need for an engineer who can own client delivery from loosely defined requirements through production deployment closely matches how I work: translate operational needs into reliable systems, validate them in production, and iterate around measurable outcomes.

At Sperse, I designed and shipped Python, FastAPI, and LangGraph conversation workflows for a multi-agent CRM platform used by more than 10,000 users. I built and consumed REST APIs across 160+ backend actions using OAuth, API key authentication, webhooks, Pydantic-validated JSON, and reusable integration patterns. I also owned configurable delivery workflows spanning YAML deployment configuration, Docker, Kubernetes, secret management, and CI/CD release gates. That work prepared me to build Attune's voice AI conversation workflows, connect CRMs and EHRs, and turn client requirements into secure implementation plans that hold up after go-live.

Production reliability has been central to my engineering work. I troubleshot agent, workflow, and integration layers with OpenTelemetry, Redis, and Temporal, adding trace-based tests that assess latency, accuracy, and safety before release. I built ingestion and export pipelines around CSV, file-based ingestion, webhooks, APIs, and SFTP-compatible delivery, while at Qualitest I supported 100K+ weekly AWS Step Functions and Lambda jobs with stronger error recovery. These experiences align directly with owning data pipelines and resolving issues across Attune's voice engine, telephony, and integration layers.

Attune's mission to connect patients and care organizations through empathetic, intelligent voice technology resonates with how I approach applied AI: trust is earned through secure, observable, and dependable systems, and success is measured by outcomes rather than activity. I would welcome the opportunity to help Attune reduce administrative barriers, close care gaps, and make client delivery faster and more repeatable. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

